<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casimir II the Just</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1138–1194</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Casimir II the Just was a Piast duke, the youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth">Bolesław III Wrymouth</a>. He inherited the Duchy of Sandomierz in 1166 and seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> and the senior throne from his brother Mieszko III in 1177. At the Congress of Łęczyca in 1180 he granted privileges to the Church and secured the hereditary succession of his line to Kraków.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casimir-ii-the-just.jpg" alt="Casimir II the Just" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Lollencja · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KIISprawiedliwy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
